window.FORGE_TERMS = {"version":1,"title":"The Smith's Naming Terms","dated":"2026-09-28","intro":"A smith who is the first in the world to pour a legend may name it. Before you do, these are the terms.","lines":[["Names are public and permanent.","Every smith in the world sees the name you give a legend. It stays on the weapon for ever and cannot be changed later."],["Name it like a smith would.","A name a smith would stamp on a blade: fierce, grim or grand is fine."],["Not allowed:","slurs, hate, or harassment of any person or group; sexual content; threats or violence aimed at real people; real people's names or personal details, yours included; brands, products, franchises, companies, or other people's characters; advertising, links or contact details; anything meant to deceive, such as posing as the game's makers or as another smith."],["The form:","2 to 28 characters; letters, digits, spaces, hyphens and apostrophes."],["Every name is checked","by the game's rules and by the Forge Oracle before it is accepted. A refused name is not written; the Oracle's name stands until you try another. A name that later turns out to break these terms is replaced with the Oracle's name, and repeated abuse loses the right to name legends."],["Your rights.","By naming a legend you give Forge Forever a permanent, worldwide, free licence to show the name in the game (on the weapon, the Ledger, the Roll of First Smiths and the Book of Kinds) and in the game's own promotion. You keep whatever rights you have in the name, and you must not use a name you have no right to use."],["Changes.","These terms may change. The version you accepted is recorded, and a new version asks you again."]],"accept_label":"I have read the Naming Terms and I accept them"};
